cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use tensorderiv in your work, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "tensorderiv: gradient, divergence, curl and Laplacian on scattered points"
authors:
  - given-names: Nikolaj Maack
    family-names: Bielefeld
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0005-4385-6444"
abstract: >-
  tensorderiv computes the gradient, divergence, curl and Laplacian of scalar, vector and tensor
  fields sampled at scattered points, without a mesh, as weighted sums of differences over each
  point's nearest neighbours, second-order accurate by default and evaluated in a compiled Rust
  core. It is a port of the Julia package DiscreteTensorDerivatives.jl by the same author, and is
  tested against it.
license: MIT
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-10-02
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.23111349"
url: "https://tensorderiv.org"
repository-code: "https://github.com/NikoBiele/tensorderiv"
keywords:
  - derivatives
  - gradient
  - meshless
  - scattered data
  - point cloud
  - numerical methods